When implementing or modifying image, video, social creative, email creative, funnel media, Open Graph media, campaign assets, brand assets, or generated visuals, read:

docs/29_VECTOR_CREATIVE_ASSET_GENERATION_MEDIA_PIPELINE.md
docs/27_VECTOR_FRONTEND_UI_UX_SALES_FUNNEL_STANDARD.md

Control / Vector product chrome stays in `docs/28`. Do not paint tenant domains with Vector identity.

First Reveal winner media and funnel asset slots follow `docs/plans/FIRST_REVEAL_TRACK.md`. Do not generate three full websites by default. Reuse C0–C7; do not fork a second creative engine.

Rules:
- Prefer authentic approved client media.
- Never regenerate the client's official logo by default.
- Keep exact text and brand marks in deterministic composition.
- Keep image and video models behind Vector-owned interfaces. Do not add generateImage to AIProvider.
- Store bytes through StorageProvider. Do not invent a second object-store adapter.
- Track client, campaign, version, provenance, rights, cost, and approval.
- Do not publish generated assets before applicable QA and approval.
- Reuse approved assets before generating new ones.
- Approved assets are immutable versions. Failed generation must fall back; never render a broken image.
